{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L106","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:106"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Durable bookkeeping for a single run."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cancelrequested","children":[{"type":"text","value":"cancelRequested?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional cancelRequested?: boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L168","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:168"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set by an explicit out-of-band cancel, to be distinguished from a mere\nclient disconnect (the two produce an identical TCP close, so intent is not\ninferable from the disconnect)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Written by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestRunCancel"},{"type":"text","value":" and read by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wasCancelRequested"},{"type":"text","value":" (both in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"../cancel"},{"type":"text","value":"). Deliberately NOT a status: recording intent is not the same as\nthe run having stopped, and only the driver knows when it has."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"detachedsince","children":[{"type":"text","value":"detachedSince?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional detachedSince?: number;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L158","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:158"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Epoch ms when the last viewer detached; absent while someone is attached.\nWritten by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s detach path ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware.ts"},{"type":"text","value":") alongside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sandboxKey"},{"type":"text","value":", when a disconnect leaves the\nagent running rather than tearing the sandbox down. A backend must\nround-trip this field: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listReclaimable"},{"type":"text","value":" depends on it, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reapDetachedRuns"},{"type":"text","value":" sweeps the candidates it\nsurfaces (see that method's doc comment)."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"driverepoch","children":[{"type":"text","value":"driverEpoch?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional driverEpoch?: number;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L178","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:178"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monotonic fencing token for the run's driver. Bumped by each host that\nsuccessfully claims the run (see "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withRunClaim"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"),\nso a superseded host can discover it lost by comparing the stored value\nagainst the one it holds."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A lock alone cannot provide this: it tells the winner it won, but gives a\nloser nothing to read. Absent on a run that was never claimed."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"error","children":[{"type":"text","value":"error?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional error?: RunError;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L137","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:137"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"finishedat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"finishedAt?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional finishedAt?: number;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L136","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:136"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"name","children":[{"type":"text","value":"name?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional name?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L133","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:133"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent name ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"researcher"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"writer"},{"type":"text","value":") when this record is a subagent."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parentrunid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"parentRunId?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional parentRunId?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L125","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:125"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parent chat run that started this child, when this record is a subagent.\nAbsent on the parent run itself."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"runid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"runId"}]},{"type":"code","value":"runId: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L107","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:107"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sandboxkey","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sandboxKey?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional sandboxKey?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L148","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:148"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compound sandbox key this run was bound to, when it ran in a sandbox.\nRecorded so a future reclaimer can identify the sandbox to tear down\nwithout re-deriving the key. Written by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s detach path\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onAbort"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"'s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware.ts"},{"type":"text","value":") at the same time as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detachedSince"},{"type":"text","value":", when a disconnect leaves the run detached rather than\ndestroying the sandbox. A backend must round-trip this field — see\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listReclaimable"},{"type":"text","value":" below for who eventually reads it."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"startedat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"startedAt"}]},{"type":"code","value":"startedAt: number;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L135","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:135"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"status","children":[{"type":"text","value":"status"}]},{"type":"code","value":"status: RunStatus;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L134","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:134"}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"subagentrunid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"subagentRunId?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional subagentRunId?: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L131","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:131"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The child's AG-UI subagentRunId, the id on its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SUBAGENT_*"},{"type":"text","value":" chunks and on\nevery chunk it streams. On a child record this equals "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":". Absent on\nthe parent run."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"threadid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"threadId"}]},{"type":"code","value":"threadId: string;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L120","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:120"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Conversation this run belongs to — the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Scope.threadId"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation jobs (a one-shot "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate()"},{"type":"text","value":" with no conversation) must not\nreuse this record by faking "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId = requestId"},{"type":"text","value":"; they need a separate\njob store. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withGenerationPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" currently does exactly that and\nlabels itself a stopgap — do not copy it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A subagent child record stores "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subagent:<subagentRunId>"},{"type":"text","value":" here, the key of\nits own transcript, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"findActiveRun"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByThread"},{"type":"text","value":" on the\nconversation never return children. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listByParentRun"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"usage?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional usage?: TokenUsage<ProviderUsageDetails>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L138","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:138"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"cancelrequested","text":"cancelRequested?","level":3},{"id":"detachedsince","text":"detachedSince?","level":3},{"id":"driverepoch","text":"driverEpoch?","level":3},{"id":"error","text":"error?","level":3},{"id":"finishedat","text":"finishedAt?","level":3},{"id":"name","text":"name?","level":3},{"id":"parentrunid","text":"parentRunId?","level":3},{"id":"runid","text":"runId","level":3},{"id":"sandboxkey","text":"sandboxKey?","level":3},{"id":"startedat","text":"startedAt","level":3},{"id":"status","text":"status","level":3},{"id":"subagentrunid","text":"subagentRunId?","level":3},{"id":"threadid","text":"threadId","level":3},{"id":"usage","text":"usage?","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:106](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L106)\n\nDurable bookkeeping for a single run.\n\n## Properties\n\n### cancelRequested?\n\n```ts\noptional cancelRequested?: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:168](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L168)\n\nSet by an explicit out-of-band cancel, to be distinguished from a mere\nclient disconnect (the two produce an identical TCP close, so intent is not\ninferable from the disconnect).\n\nWritten by `requestRunCancel` and read by `wasCancelRequested` (both in\n`../cancel`). Deliberately NOT a status: recording intent is not the same as\nthe run having stopped, and only the driver knows when it has.\n\n***\n\n### detachedSince?\n\n```ts\noptional detachedSince?: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:158](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L158)\n\nEpoch ms when the last viewer detached; absent while someone is attached.\nWritten by `withSandbox`'s detach path (`onAbort` in `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s\n`middleware.ts`) alongside `sandboxKey`, when a disconnect leaves the\nagent running rather than tearing the sandbox down. A backend must\nround-trip this field: `listReclaimable` depends on it, and\n`@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s `reapDetachedRuns` sweeps the candidates it\nsurfaces (see that method's doc comment).\n\n***\n\n### driverEpoch?\n\n```ts\noptional driverEpoch?: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:178](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L178)\n\nMonotonic fencing token for the run's driver. Bumped by each host that\nsuccessfully claims the run (see `withRunClaim` in `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`),\nso a superseded host can discover it lost by comparing the stored value\nagainst the one it holds.\n\nA lock alone cannot provide this: it tells the winner it won, but gives a\nloser nothing to read. Absent on a run that was never claimed.\n\n***\n\n### error?\n\n```ts\noptional error?: RunError;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:137](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L137)\n\n***\n\n### finishedAt?\n\n```ts\noptional finishedAt?: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:136](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L136)\n\n***\n\n### name?\n\n```ts\noptional name?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:133](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L133)\n\nAgent name (`researcher`, `writer`) when this record is a subagent.\n\n***\n\n### parentRunId?\n\n```ts\noptional parentRunId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:125](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L125)\n\nParent chat run that started this child, when this record is a subagent.\nAbsent on the parent run itself.\n\n***\n\n### runId\n\n```ts\nrunId: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:107](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L107)\n\n***\n\n### sandboxKey?\n\n```ts\noptional sandboxKey?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:148](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L148)\n\nCompound sandbox key this run was bound to, when it ran in a sandbox.\nRecorded so a future reclaimer can identify the sandbox to tear down\nwithout re-deriving the key. Written by `withSandbox`'s detach path\n(`onAbort` in `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s `middleware.ts`) at the same time as\n`detachedSince`, when a disconnect leaves the run detached rather than\ndestroying the sandbox. A backend must round-trip this field — see\n`listReclaimable` below for who eventually reads it.\n\n***\n\n### startedAt\n\n```ts\nstartedAt: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:135](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L135)\n\n***\n\n### status\n\n```ts\nstatus: RunStatus;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:134](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L134)\n\n***\n\n### subagentRunId?\n\n```ts\noptional subagentRunId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:131](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L131)\n\nThe child's AG-UI subagentRunId, the id on its `SUBAGENT_*` chunks and on\nevery chunk it streams. On a child record this equals `runId`. Absent on\nthe parent run.\n\n***\n\n### threadId\n\n```ts\nthreadId: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:120](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L120)\n\nConversation this run belongs to — the `Scope.threadId`.\n\nGeneration jobs (a one-shot `generate()` with no conversation) must not\nreuse this record by faking `threadId = requestId`; they need a separate\njob store. `withGenerationPersistence` currently does exactly that and\nlabels itself a stopgap — do not copy it.\n\nA subagent child record stores `subagent:<subagentRunId>` here, the key of\nits own transcript, so `findActiveRun` and `listByThread` on the\nconversation never return children. Use `listByParentRun`.\n\n***\n\n### usage?\n\n```ts\noptional usage?: TokenUsage<ProviderUsageDetails>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:138](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L138)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: RunRecord\ntitle: RunRecord\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:106](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L106)\n\nDurable bookkeeping for a single run.\n\n## Properties\n\n### cancelRequested?\n\n```ts\noptional cancelRequested?: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:168](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L168)\n\nSet by an explicit out-of-band cancel, to be distinguished from a mere\nclient disconnect (the two produce an identical TCP close, so intent is not\ninferable from the disconnect).\n\nWritten by `requestRunCancel` and read by `wasCancelRequested` (both in\n`../cancel`). Deliberately NOT a status: recording intent is not the same as\nthe run having stopped, and only the driver knows when it has.\n\n***\n\n### detachedSince?\n\n```ts\noptional detachedSince?: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:158](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L158)\n\nEpoch ms when the last viewer detached; absent while someone is attached.\nWritten by `withSandbox`'s detach path (`onAbort` in `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s\n`middleware.ts`) alongside `sandboxKey`, when a disconnect leaves the\nagent running rather than tearing the sandbox down. A backend must\nround-trip this field: `listReclaimable` depends on it, and\n`@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s `reapDetachedRuns` sweeps the candidates it\nsurfaces (see that method's doc comment).\n\n***\n\n### driverEpoch?\n\n```ts\noptional driverEpoch?: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:178](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L178)\n\nMonotonic fencing token for the run's driver. Bumped by each host that\nsuccessfully claims the run (see `withRunClaim` in `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`),\nso a superseded host can discover it lost by comparing the stored value\nagainst the one it holds.\n\nA lock alone cannot provide this: it tells the winner it won, but gives a\nloser nothing to read. Absent on a run that was never claimed.\n\n***\n\n### error?\n\n```ts\noptional error?: RunError;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:137](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L137)\n\n***\n\n### finishedAt?\n\n```ts\noptional finishedAt?: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:136](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L136)\n\n***\n\n### name?\n\n```ts\noptional name?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:133](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L133)\n\nAgent name (`researcher`, `writer`) when this record is a subagent.\n\n***\n\n### parentRunId?\n\n```ts\noptional parentRunId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:125](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L125)\n\nParent chat run that started this child, when this record is a subagent.\nAbsent on the parent run itself.\n\n***\n\n### runId\n\n```ts\nrunId: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:107](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L107)\n\n***\n\n### sandboxKey?\n\n```ts\noptional sandboxKey?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:148](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L148)\n\nCompound sandbox key this run was bound to, when it ran in a sandbox.\nRecorded so a future reclaimer can identify the sandbox to tear down\nwithout re-deriving the key. Written by `withSandbox`'s detach path\n(`onAbort` in `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s `middleware.ts`) at the same time as\n`detachedSince`, when a disconnect leaves the run detached rather than\ndestroying the sandbox. A backend must round-trip this field — see\n`listReclaimable` below for who eventually reads it.\n\n***\n\n### startedAt\n\n```ts\nstartedAt: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:135](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L135)\n\n***\n\n### status\n\n```ts\nstatus: RunStatus;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:134](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L134)\n\n***\n\n### subagentRunId?\n\n```ts\noptional subagentRunId?: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:131](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L131)\n\nThe child's AG-UI subagentRunId, the id on its `SUBAGENT_*` chunks and on\nevery chunk it streams. On a child record this equals `runId`. Absent on\nthe parent run.\n\n***\n\n### threadId\n\n```ts\nthreadId: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:120](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L120)\n\nConversation this run belongs to — the `Scope.threadId`.\n\nGeneration jobs (a one-shot `generate()` with no conversation) must not\nreuse this record by faking `threadId = requestId`; they need a separate\njob store. `withGenerationPersistence` currently does exactly that and\nlabels itself a stopgap — do not copy it.\n\nA subagent child record stores `subagent:<subagentRunId>` here, the key of\nits own transcript, so `findActiveRun` and `listByThread` on the\nconversation never return children. Use `listByParentRun`.\n\n***\n\n### usage?\n\n```ts\noptional usage?: TokenUsage<ProviderUsageDetails>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:138](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L138)\n"}
